ore":0.0,"weight":0.1},"market":{"score":0.0,"weight":0.1}},"data_summaries":{"sect":["Its 13% operating margin trails the Financial Services median (29%) by 16pp, so it is a below-average operator in its field.","It captures well under its share of sector profits (0.49x its revenue share).","It accounts for 0.7% of sector revenue and 0.4% of sector operating profit.","Over five years it has been losing share of the sector profit pool (-4.3% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.02 across 512 companies in the universe; the top four hold 20% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a strong uptrend, up 35% over the past year excluding the latest month, though it has pulled back 10% over the last three months.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 15% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 21% and a beta of 0.71, it is more defensive than the market.","About $34.3M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 51% in the 2020 crash, 31% in the 2022 bear market and 78% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $54.26 (margin of safety -32%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 3%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $43.48 to $69.96 (P10-P90).","On multiples it looks expensive against Financial Services peers: P/E 18.6 vs 12.2 and P/FCF 21.1 vs 12.9 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 49% above its 10-year median.","The Street target $64.53 on average, 10% below the price.","The price implies 3.0% annual cash-flow growth, 5pp more than the model expects."],"prof":["ROIC of 21% clears the cost of capital of 8.0% by 13pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have been steady (CV 0.17).","It converts 6% of revenue into free cash flow.","It earns a 15% return on equity."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 18.7% over 3 years and -1.5% over 5 years, so growth is accelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 31%).","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 2.8% on average.","Analysts expect 7.6% long-term annual earnings growth."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.1%), and institutions hold 56%.","It returns 6.7% a year to shareholders (3.0% in buybacks and 3.8% in dividends).","It has paid a dividend for 25 consecutive years, raising it 7.8% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 32,151 employees, each generates about $922K of revenue, 1.8x the Financial Services median, and productivity has risen 3.6% a year.","That works out to $58K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $2.5M (3x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (2/10, lower is better)."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":29,"head":"Avoid: priced 32% above its fair value of $54.26.","pros":["ROE 15.4% vs cost of equity 8.3%","12-1 month momentum +35%","Returns 6.7% a year to shareholders"],"cons":["Model rating PASS (composite 12, gates 4/14)","Trades 32% above fair value of $54.26","Revenue shrank 1.5%/yr over 5y","Piotroski F-score 2/9","P/E 18.6x vs sector 12.2x"],"flags":["Priced 32% above its fair value of $54.26","The model rates it PASS"],"need":[],"buy_below":46.12,"vc":{"base":54.26,"base_src":"dcf","bear":43.48,"bull":69.96,"alt_median":52.86,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.0379,"dispersion":0.0298,"level":"HIGH","why":[]},"med":{"pe":12.155,"ev_ebitda":10.862,"pfcf":12.9041,"pb":1.3934,"roic":0.116,"gross_margin":0.4181,"fcf_margin":0.2507,"div_yield":0.0265}},"ticker":"SLF","date":"2026-11-06"}